","accent":"#9e3b28","body":"Roman fast food. The round holes in the counter held dolia — big jars of stew, wine and hot food. There are about eighty of these in Pompeii, because most flats had no kitchen and no chimney. The counter is faced in broken scraps of marble, which is exactly how the real ones look."}},{"id":"34033aa1-1797-47a5-acf2-9e54bd09f55e","createdAt":1786942188989,"transform":{"position":[-34,-0.0007424196601544253,-8],"rotation":[0,1.5707963267948966,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"forum-colonnade","options":{"bays":7,"spacing":8,"height":15,"seed":29}},{"id":"ea4e38f1-93c0-483e-ba9c-21644272b5bd","createdAt":1786942188991,"transform":{"position":[34,-0.0004912406035710859,-8],"rotation":[0,-1.5707963267948966,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"forum-colonnade","options":{"bays":7,"spacing":8,"height":15,"seed":33}},{"id":"16df400b-0bd8-4029-ba4d-6e6d2264376e","createdAt":1786942188992,"transform":{"position":[-18,-8.881784197001252e-16,4],"rotation":[0,0.17809293823119754,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"The town square","title":"The Forum","accent":"#c98b3a","body":"Law courts, temples, the market and the town council all opened onto this one paved square, and no carts were allowed in it. Every Roman town of any size was laid out around one, which is why a Roman who had never been here would still have known exactly where to find things."}},{"id":"ad6bfb3b-4b49-46c7-9f72-9a45ad78c71c","createdAt":1786942188993,"transform":{"position":[86,1.1004008985857312,-58],"rotation":[0,0,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"amphitheatre","options":{"radiusX":42,"radiusZ":34,"height":15,"seed":31}},{"id":"b617fbc3-609a-49cd-89c3-0d2841488376","createdAt":1786942188994,"transform":{"position":[52,0.00021155665441385807,-34],"rotation":[0,-0.3603579705247931,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"Built about 70 BC","title":"The Amphitheatre","accent":"#8a4630","body":"The oldest stone amphitheatre that still stands anywhere — a hundred and fifty years older than the Colosseum. It held 20,000 people, which is more than lived in the town. In AD 59 a riot broke out here between locals and visitors from Nuceria and the Senate banned games for ten years."}},{"id":"f9f8e05f-742c-4e63-8f10-20c19a217543","createdAt":1786942188995,"transform":{"position":[-13,-0.13849170771957775,-46],"rotation":[0,0.08645065168737405,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"fresco-wall","options":{"width":15,"height":10,"seed":41}},{"id":"af732670-30b4-4302-90a6-81e641e1a30b","createdAt":1786942188997,"transform":{"position":[14,-0.19793515528384642,-52],"rotation":[0,-0.08950381835161035,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"fresco-wall","options":{"width":13,"height":9,"seed":45}},{"id":"3a967542-28db-4dd7-9fcc-ab2399fd0b7e","createdAt":1786942188998,"transform":{"position":[-4,-0.021646605919945827,-40],"rotation":[0,0.027770636593421036,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"info-placard","options":{"eyebrow":"What the walls looked like","title":"Pompeian red","accent":"#9e3b28","body":"Almost every room in town was painted, floor to ceiling, in deep red and ochre fields divided by thin painted architecture with a small picture in the middle. The colour is so associated with this one town that painters still call it Pompeian red."}},{"id":"ab3ab724-0e31-4031-bc09-d3cbc7558c0d","createdAt":1786942188999,"transform":{"position":[-46,-0.14880005949962039,30],"rotation":[0,0.6,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"plaster-cast","options":{"pose":"curled","seed":37}},{"id":"a41e94dd-159f-4862-aa52-5e36ba75d637","createdAt":1786942189000,"transform":{"position":[-50,-0.20762374840125908,24],"rotation":[0,-0.9,0],"scale":[1,1,1]},"kind":"preset-prop","prop":"plaster-cast","options":{"pose":"curled","seed":39}},{"id":"7639d70e-54f2-4152-b08b-c7330d7e32c0","createdAt":178